   "reason": "The key on the king's diagonal is usually defended, which makes the bishop capture suicide; with the shield up she takes it anyway, absorbs the recapture, keeps the capture-stun and takes the king on the next move. | A rook's attack set is a whole rank and file, so detonating the Twin clears both lines at once — the widest non-queen blast, and the strongest way to open a corridor into the pen in one free action.",
